WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.316
A person who uses a screen reader opens an invitation

00:00:03.316 --> 00:00:06.632
to a public session. The screen reader announces one thing:

00:00:06.632 --> 00:00:09.948
image. The date, the time, the link and the number

00:00:09.948 --> 00:00:13.265
to call for accommodations are all inside a picture of

00:00:13.265 --> 00:00:16.581
a flyer. The person cannot find any of them. A

00:00:16.581 --> 00:00:19.897
sighted colleague would see a clear, attractive invitation. The author

00:00:19.897 --> 00:00:20.560
meant well.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.016
The barrier was built in at the start, and it

00:00:24.016 --> 00:00:26.190
can be removed at the start too.

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.449
The rules are now specific. The U.S. Department of Justice

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:34.357
rule under Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act

00:00:34.357 --> 00:00:38.266
sets WCAG 2.1 Level AA as the standard for state

00:00:38.266 --> 00:00:42.174
and local government web content. That includes new PDFs, Word

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:46.083
files and slides. For a state agency, the compliance date

00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:49.991
is April 26, 2027. Minnesota law already requires state agencies

00:00:49.991 --> 00:00:53.900
to follow accessibility standards built on WCAG and Section 508.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:58.650
And the ADA duty of effective communication applies today.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.698
Most failures are common and fixable. A 2026 scan of

00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:06.397
a million home pages found detected failures on almost 96

00:01:06.397 --> 00:01:10.095
percent. Low-contrast text was the most common problem, followed by

00:01:10.095 --> 00:01:13.793
missing descriptions for images, unlabeled form fields and empty links.

00:01:13.793 --> 00:01:17.492
Use an accessible template. Put key details in ordinary text.

00:01:17.492 --> 00:01:21.190
Use real heading styles. Name each link for where it

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:21.560
goes.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:25.843
Run the checker, then move through the file using only

00:01:25.843 --> 00:01:26.630
the keyboard.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.300
Plain language is part of access. In an IRS field

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.620
experiment, people who had not claimed a tax credit received

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.940
notices. Simpler, clearer notices led to substantial additional claims. Messages

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.260
meant to reassure people did not. So put the action

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.580
first. Say what to do, by when, and how to

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.900
get help. Required legal language can follow, under short headings.

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:50.721
Be honest about limits. In one randomized trial, a plain

00:01:50.721 --> 00:01:54.193
version improved understanding of one health recommendation by almost 20

00:01:54.193 --> 00:01:57.664
points, but barely changed understanding of another. Plain language helps

00:01:57.664 --> 00:02:01.136
most when the original is hard. Test drafts with a

00:02:01.136 --> 00:02:04.607
few readers and ask them to tell you, in their

00:02:04.607 --> 00:02:06.690
own words, what they must do.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.278
Meetings need the same care. Send materials ahead. Arrange captions

00:02:10.278 --> 00:02:13.515
and interpreters. Offer more than one way to take part.

00:02:13.515 --> 00:02:16.753
A review of more than 100 studies found captions help

00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:19.990
many viewers understand and remember. Finally, name one person at

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:23.228
the start who will pause the meeting if access fails.

00:02:23.228 --> 00:02:26.465
When the captions stop, that person speaks up, and no

00:02:26.465 --> 00:02:27.760
one is left behind.
